id: pm-eg5u1n
title: Return a typed assurance refusal for unknown declaration reads instead of high-priority Sentry faults
description: "Live Sentry PM-CLI-3P (154999406) has two high-priority handled TypeError events at 2026-10-20 20:18:50/57 UTC for assurance measurement repository-static-quality not found. getAssuranceDeclaration throws raw TypeError, while the existing transport already handles AssuranceEvaluationRefusalError for ordinary assurance input refusals. The historical gate/trigger fix pm-9yhl2v is closed and shipped; this distinct declaration-read path remains untyped."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-20T20:40:15.393Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T21:57:15.087Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T21:13:59.070Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-20T21:13:59.070Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "Reuse the existing typed SDK refusal, cover all declaration kinds through public SDK and action transport; prove failing-before and valid reads remain intact; verify fresh CLI/Sentry behavior after review and merge without suppressing genuine runtime errors."
parent: pm-1jzupz
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "Public SDK governance entrypoint, CLI/MCP assurance show transports"
repro_steps: In an isolated initialized tracker call getAssuranceDeclaration or runAssuranceAction show for a missing measurement/assertion/gate; compare direct SDK error subtype and structured action/CLI response.
resolution: getAssuranceDeclaration now throws the existing TypeError-compatible AssuranceEvaluationRefusalError. Show and promote normalize that expected refusal to invalid_argument_value / assurance_evaluation_refused while unexpected runtime faults remain unchanged.
expected_result: Unknown measurement/assertion/gate reads and missing promotion assertions produce actionable usage refusals instead of unexpected-fault Sentry events.
actual_result: Seven regression cases fail before and all 29 focused SDK/action/MCP cases pass after. Built public Node and Bun SDK probes preserve both class identities; both CLIs return usage exit 2 for all declaration kinds. The original two-event Sentry group awaits merged-main live verification before retirement; this source fix is Unreleased.
affected_version: 2026.10.20
component: SDK assurance declaration reads
